sieve-filter-v2
; melody-ending-v1 on every note set (notes104 and notes2): the last event is a note on the tonic
; (any octave), at least `hold` long by its real length in sixteenths (LENGTH, SIXTEENTHS). On
; notes104 it is exactly melody-ending-v1.
id        melody-ending
version   2
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes*
describe  The last note is the tonic, held at least so long, on every note set.
param     tonic  choice  C C,C#,D,D#,E,F,F#,G,G#,A,A#,B the note to end on
param     hold   choice  e s,e,E,q,Q,h,H,w the shortest the last note may be

states    2
start     0
accept    1
for s 0 1
  for d 0 {DURATIONS - 1}
    t {s} @{d} 0
    for p 1 {PITCHES}
      if {(LOW + p - 1) % 12 == tonic && LENGTH(d) >= SIXTEENTHS(hold)}
        t {s} @{p * DURATIONS + d} 1
      else
        t {s} @{p * DURATIONS + d} 0
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
